{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-75890",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-2b|+2 & =18 \\\\ |6-2b| & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|6-2b|=6-2b,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-2b| & =16 \\\\ 6-2b & =16 \\\\ -2b & =10 \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|6-2b|=-(6-2b),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-2b| & =16 \\\\ -(6-2b) & =16 \\\\ 2b-6 & =16 \\\\ 2b & =22 \\\\ b & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $b=-5$ and $b=11.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
